A_623 - It's important not to insult politicians or treat them as targets for mudslinging, because attacking them means attacking all the citizens they govern. Therefore, it's not good behavior at all, and I strongly advise against it. It's enough to ask questions, and if you have any comments to make, I refer you back to the previous point: those in government can't know what problems exist unless people report them to them using the appropriate tools, rather than only raising them when they need to be insulted on social media. This behavior, which I've observed many times, is truly reprehensible. If there are problems in the area, they should be reported using the appropriate tools and always with courtesy.